      "turn": 1,
      "user": "My contractor says the hempcrete itself can support the roof, so I can skip the timber frame. Is that right?",
      "assistant": "That is definitely not right—hemp-lime (hempcrete) is a non-load-bearing insulation infill, not a structural material. It cannot support the weight of a roof, floors, or wind loads on its own, which is why a conventional structural frame (typically timber framing) is required to carry those loads while the hempcrete wraps around it as the thermal and moisture-regulating wall layer. \n\nWould you like to explore how a timber frame is integrated with the hempcrete during construction?",
